WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.668
On the client card, “Insured items”

2
00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.790
keeps the client’s vehicles, home and business in one place,

3
00:00:05.976 --> 00:00:09.354
with values, drivers, dates and the linked policies.

4
00:00:09.912 --> 00:00:11.699
Press “Add item”.

5
00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:17.280
For a vehicle, registration, make, no-claims years and drivers;

6
00:00:17.466 --> 00:00:19.498
a follow-up is created fourteen days

7
00:00:19.498 --> 00:00:21.854
before the MOT and the road-tax date.

8
00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:27.624
For a home, area, year built, rebuild value and contents value.

9
00:00:28.724 --> 00:00:31.835
If the area times the cost per square metre comes out

10
00:00:31.835 --> 00:00:36.130
higher than the recorded rebuild value, the CRM flags it:

11
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:39.126
worth checking with the client and the insurer.

12
00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:43.503
It is indicative, not advice and not a valuation.

13
00:00:44.603 --> 00:00:47.285
A premium the insurer could not collect is recorded

14
00:00:47.285 --> 00:00:50.233
on the policy with “Record overdue premium”,

15
00:00:50.536 --> 00:00:54.064
or you bring in the insurer’s list with “Import insurer list”:

16
00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.618
you choose the policy number, amount and due date columns,

17
00:00:57.618 --> 00:01:02.354
and rows match only on the exact policy number, never by guess.

18
00:01:03.454 --> 00:01:06.669
If the amount stays open longer than the days set in Settings,

19
00:01:06.763 --> 00:01:10.744
fifteen by default, the policy shows “Risk of lapse”.

20
00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:13.681
The reminder to the client opens as a draft,

21
00:01:13.775 --> 00:01:15.703
and you close the item as “Paid”

22
00:01:15.703 --> 00:01:17.072
or “Lapsed”.

23
00:01:18.172 --> 00:01:19.297
In the next lesson:

24
00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:21.480
how to ask your clients for feedback.
